The cost for the remaining \( 100 - 10 = 90 \) kilometers is \( 150 - 90 = 60 \) dollars.

The taxi cost per kilometer for the remaining 90 kilometers is \( \frac{60}{90} = \frac{2}{3} \) hours/km.

Now, if Anna traveled 150 kilometers, the cost for the first 10 kilometers would be \( 90 \)  eues.

The remaining distance would be \( 150 - 10 = 140 \) kilometers.

The cost for the remaining 140 kilometers would be \( 140 \times \frac{2}{3} = \frac{280}{3} \) euros.

