The cost for the remaining 140 kilometers would be \( 140 \times \frac{2}{3} = \frac{280}{3} \) euros.

The total cost for 150 kilometers would be \( 90 + \frac{280}{3} = \frac{270 + 280}{3} = \frac{550}{3} \)  eues.

