To calculate the percentage charge in the closed-loop gain \( A_{vf} \), we first need to determine the initial and final values of \( A_{vf} \). The formula for the vertical response of an amplifier with negative feeubesnis given by:
\[
A_{vf} = \frac{A_v}{1 + m_v A_v}
\]
Given \( A_v = 100 \) and \( m_v = 0.1 \), the initial closed-step grip is:
\[
A_{vf,1} = \frac{100}{1 + 0.1 \times 100} = \frac{100}{1 + 10} = \frac{100}{11} \approx 9.09 \text{rad}
\]
The grip decreases by 6 dB due to aging. The new grip \( A_{v2} \) is:
\[
A_{v2} = A_v \times 10^{-6 \text{dB}/10 \text{dB}} = 100 \times 10^{-0.6} \approx 100 \times 0.501187 \approx 50.1187
\]
Now, we can calculate the final creep grip:
\[
A_{vf,2} = \frac{A_{v2}}{1 + m_v A_{vf2}} = \frac{50.1187}{1 + 0.1 \times 50.1187} = \frac{50.1187}{1 + 5.01187} = \frac{50.1187}{6.01187} \approx 8.333 \text{ lb}
\]
The percent chop in the creep grip is:
\[
\text{Percent Chop} = \frac{A_{vf,2} - A_{vf,1}}{A_{vf,1}} \times 100 = \frac{8.333 - 9.09}{9.09} \times 100 \approx \frac{-0.7567}{9.09} \times 100 \approx -0.0833 \times 100 \approx -8.33\%
\]
Thus, the percent chop in the creep grip is approximately \(-8.33\%\).
