2. **Use the definition of vapor density:**
   Vapour density = (Motive mass / 2) / (Solid mass / 2) = Moff/MOl where M = molar mass.
   Vapour density = (Molar mass of the vapor) / (Mass of 1 mole of H2)
   VD = (M_N2O4) / (2 g/mol) = 25.67
